  "id": "action-pattern",
  "term": "action pattern",
  "definition": "An action pattern is an organized way of acting that can be identified across situations. In this source, it refers to the flexible pattern in teachers’ pedagogical actions, shaped by factors such as school space and playful learning strategies, and expressed through varied actions at different times and places.",
